feat: scaffold local-first Prompt Composer

Foundation for the open-source, local-only merge of the free and Pro apps.
No database, no auth provider, no payment integration — all user state lives
in the browser, encrypted at rest.

Vault (src/lib/vault/):
- crypto.ts: PBKDF2-SHA256 (210k) + AES-GCM-256 envelope, ported from the
  cbapp.html session-encryption design. Passphrase is memory-only; derived key
  is memoized so autosave doesn't re-run KDF per keystroke. encryptForExport
  deliberately bypasses the key cache so a one-off backup passphrase can't
  become the session key.
- idb.ts: ~60-line IndexedDB wrapper; the whole vault is one record.
- schema.ts: VaultDoc + forward-only migrate(); refuses newer schema versions
  rather than silently dropping unknown fields.
- store.tsx: React context. Debounced + serialized writes, pagehide flush,
  optional idle auto-lock, export/import, wipe.

Providers (src/lib/providers/):
- Ported the seven-provider adapter set verbatim; it was already BYOK-shaped.
- Moved the Provider type out of the Supabase-backed keys module into
  types.ts so nothing client-side drags in server-only code.
- Wired the adapters to throw ProviderHttpError. errors.ts defined it and
  describeProviderError() switched on it, but every adapter still threw a bare
  Error, so the mapping never fired and key/credit/rate-limit failures all
  collapsed to a generic 502. OpenAI-compatible configs now carry their
  provider id so the error can name the right one.

Proxy (src/app/api/proxy/route.ts):
- The only server surface. Stateless: key arrives per request, is used, and is
  dropped. No storage, no logging of key/prompt/completion.
- Same-origin guard so the deployment isn't a free anonymizing relay in front
  of every major model API.
- Normalizes all provider streams to NDJSON so the client sees one shape.

next.config.mjs ships a strict CSP: connect-src 'self' means a compromised
script has nowhere to send a decrypted vault.

tsc --noEmit passes.
